    "gold.dim_block_group": {
      "title": "Block group dimension",
      "description": "One row per 2025 TIGER block group in the in-scope states (FIPS 12/24/48) with TIGER's stored ALAND/AWATER in m2 and the ACS 2023 5-year population B01003_001E. density_per_km2 = population / (aland_m2 / 1e6) -- arithmetic on a stored area, not a geometric operation, so no projection is involved (it would be EPSG:5070 if it were). There is deliberately no dim_tract: tract_geoid is bg_geoid[:11] by the Census's own GEOID construction and a table whose only content is a substring of another key is not a dimension. Population is the ONLY ACS variable loaded: income, tenure, vehicles and commute are the protected-class proxies ASSIGNMENT.md Part 4 warns about, and a feature that was never loaded cannot leak into a lead score.",
